<title>UK: Hyder in port project in Xiamen, China.</title>
<headline>Hyder in port project in Xiamen, China.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The engineering consultancy division of British utility group Hyder Plc said on Thursday it had won a project contract to prepare a masterplan for the port of Xiamen, China, on behalf of the Asian Development Bank.</p>
<p>In a statement Hyder said the development and implementation planning work, which started in mid-January, would take about four months and was worth around $600,000.</p>
<p>&quot;Our assignment is particularly interesting at this time with the recent announcement of an agreement between the People's Republic of China and Taiwan to establish direct sea links across the Taiwan Strait after a 48-year ban,&quot; it added.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
